{
  "id": "control.button",
  "kind": "block",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "category": "control",
  "name": "button",
  "state": "stable",
  "knowledge": {
    "purpose": "Clickable trigger for an action, navigation, or form submit — primary interactive control",
    "useCases": [
      "Form submit",
      "Primary call-to-action on a marketing page",
      "Modal confirm or cancel",
      "Wizard step navigation on one page — action setState step, sections gated by visibleWhen"
    ],
    "composesWith": [
      "form.form",
      "layout.container",
      "layout.section",
      "platform/navigation",
      "platform/interaction"
    ],
    "antiPatterns": [
      "Plain text styled as a button — use control.link for navigation",
      "Multiple primary buttons in the same visual area",
      "Buttons that are actually on/off switches — a button fires an action and holds no state; a visible two-way choice is form.segmented-control",
      "href and action on the same button — href navigates first and the action never runs; give a button one job"
    ],
    "implementation": "CLICK WRITES STATE — `action`: one action or a list, run in order on the click (never on other events). Same shape as a behavior's actions: setState {key, value}, refresh {sourceId}, refreshAll, showBlock/hideBlock {blockId}, navigate {url}.\nWizard on one page: initialState {\"step\": 1}; sections carry visibleWhen \"{{state.step == 1}}\", \"{{state.step == 2}}\" …; \"Next\" → \"action\": [{\"type\":\"setState\",\"key\":\"step\",\"value\":2},{\"type\":\"setState\",\"key\":\"stepError\",\"value\":\"\"}]; \"Back\" → {\"type\":\"setState\",\"key\":\"step\",\"value\":1}.\nInside a repeat the action resolves per row, so {\"type\":\"setState\",\"key\":\"selectedId\",\"value\":\"{{item.id}}\"} writes that row's id. To open a detail PAGE from a row use a link instead: href \"/product?id={{item.id}}\" — the published app seeds state.id from the address.\nIf href is set it wins: the button navigates and the action does not run. Where it opens: `target` (_self | _blank) decides; unset, an external absolute http(s) address opens in a new tab (noopener, noreferrer) like the link block, while relative addresses, # and same-origin addresses stay in this tab; mailto: and tel: are unchanged. Without href the button emits its click and the runtime runs the action.\n\nLabel weight follows the theme voice: font-weight reads var(--pw-font-weight-heading, 600) — a fixed 500 made every theme’s controls look alike while headingWeight runs 400–800.\nCorners: border-radius reads var(--pw-button-radius, var(--pw-border-radius)) — a theme sets --pw-button-radius (styleVariables) for pill or square buttons without changing the corners of cards and inputs; unset, buttons follow the theme corner."
  },
  "definition": {
